// Tiled f32 GEMM for the transposed-weight layout:
//   Y[M,N] = A[M,K] @ B[N,K]^T (+ bias[N]),  alpha = beta = 1, transA = 0, transB = 1.
//
// A 64x64 output tile is divided into per-invocation result blocks. The row-block
// and K-block constants select how many results reuse each
// staged weight tile while staying within workgroup-storage limits.
// The workgroup remains 16x16 for every configuration:
//   - K = inFeatures and N = outFeatures are baked constants (always known here);
//   - M is the dispatch-time `params.M`, grid-strided over the M- and N-tile
//     axes so one compiled pipeline serves every M and covers tile counts past
//     the maxComputeWorkgroupsPerDimension limit;
//   - B is the transposed [N,K] weight, so logical B[k,n] = b[n*K + k].
// M, N, and K are fully bounds-checked; no shape alignment is required.
