// Cosine-sum window:
//   w = a0 - a1*cos(phase) + a2*cos(2*phase), phase = 2*pi*n/N
// Compiled coefficients select Hann, Hamming, or Blackman. N (params.denom) is
// the window length for a periodic window, or length - 1 for a symmetric window.
//
// The implementation keeps n/N as a rational turn, evaluates an explicit
// unit-circle polynomial, and forms a0 - a1*c with one rounding through
// fma(-a1, c, a0). WGSL builtin transcendental accuracy is
// implementation-defined, and a rounded multiply followed by subtraction would
// double-round. Grid strides cover large windows with a clamped dispatch.
{{ env.wgsl.resourceDeclarations }}

