// com.microsoft.FusedMatMul subgroup-matrix specialization: Y = alpha * op(A) @ op(B).
// transA and transB transpose the corresponding matrix operand on load.
// Dense batches map through workgroup_id.z, and M-tail rows are guarded by row_limit.
// The row count M arrives per call in `params.M`, so one pipeline serves every M;
// K, N and the batch layout compile in.
// A K % 32 == 0 gate keeps the reduction loop whole; N is free of the 64-wide column
// tile because nTailSafe clamps the trailing tile's B columns to N - 1 and guards
// every store on col < N. Both operands stage through workgroup memory, so
// subgroupMatrixLoad only ever reads the full tile_A/tile_B arrays and never sees a
// partial 8x8 tile at any M or N. The clamp is not interchangeable with a zero fill:
// an out-of-bounds subgroupMatrixLoad resets to offset 0 and returns a different
// valid tile, and a duplicated real column keeps the discarded accumulators finite.
// The batch is required to match between A and B (no broadcast) because a_base and
// b_base both index by the same workgroup_id.z.
