// Flash-style tiled online-softmax attention over the projected QKV working
// buffers. One workgroup owns QUERY_TILE consecutive query tokens of one
// (batch, head) and sweeps the key axis in tiles of WG keys, each invocation
// owning one key of the tile. A key row is loaded once and scored against every
// query of the tile, so one pass over the key and value streams serves QUERY_TILE
// queries instead of one.
//
// Q lives in [batch, sequence, heads, paddedHeadSize] and K/V in
// [2, batch, total, heads, paddedHeadSize]; both are read as vec4 words, which is
// what the padded head size buys. The padding lanes hold zero, so they add
// nothing to a score and nothing to a value sum. The op output has the UNPADDED
// [batch, sequence, heads * headSize] layout, so the epilogue stores scalars.
//
// Every mask rule — padding, the mask_filter_value fill, and causal exclusion —
// arrives as one additive f32 table with broadcast strides, so this kernel has no
// mask-shape or unidirectional branch.
const HEAD_DIM_V4: u32 = {{ headPadV4 }}u;
const HEAD_SIZE: u32 = {{ headSize }}u;
const NUM_HEADS: u32 = {{ numHeads }}u;
const QKV_HIDDEN_V4: u32 = NUM_HEADS * HEAD_DIM_V4;
